## Final verdict: **NARROW — conditional**

Do **not** freeze v0.2.1 as written. Recommend implementation and unit tests only after the remaining contracts are corrected and explicitly approved.

| Question | Verdict | Main finding |
|---|---|---|
| Q1 Total decision | disagree | Boolean fallback mishandles missing/unassessable states; L preservation is improved. |
| Q2 P/PA contract | conditional | Separate baselines are correct; finish scope, null handling and noncausal interpretation. |
| Q3 P gate | agree | Still weak; appropriate only as a sensitivity screen. |
| Q4 M contract | conditional | POS AND NORM is appropriate; cohort, numerical-failure and replay details remain. |
| Q5 Statistics | conditional | Core mathematics is sound; complete-case and deterministic execution rules need tightening. |
| Q6 Debug | conditional | Exposure controls improve; enforce isolation, bounds and artifact separation. |
| Q7 Cap/artifacts | disagree | Debug plus the full run can total **16 units/1,220 updates**, exceeding **12/1,200**. |
| Q8 Must-fix | agree | Five ranked operational contracts remain open. |
| Q9 Implementation/tests | conditional | Corrected freeze and explicit authorization first. |
| Q10 Mechanics debug | conditional | Only after tests, budget reconciliation and separate authorization. |
| Q11 Three-seed/B0-B | agree | Separate approval gates must remain. |
| Q12 Final disposition | conditional | **NARROW; no execution approval.** |

### Must-fix, ranked

1. **Decision/missingness:** explicit unavailable states, missing-seed handling, small-N checks and consistent path-failure precedence.
2. **Budget:** reconcile debug-inclusive arithmetic and enforce shared time, unit, update and thread accounting.
3. **Cohorts:** define intersections across required arms, seeds, endpoints and M variants; separate structural exclusions from integrity failures.
4. **Execution semantics:** freeze matched P/PA step0 cropping, retention null guards, donor handling, bootstrap and heavy-tail definitions.
5. **Artifacts/tests:** separate unit/debug/pooled outputs, persist replayable checkpoints, and keep pure contract tests outside model-dependent skips.

Only the designated report was written; tracked files remain unchanged. No training, evaluation or tests were run. **Phase 6, B0-B/B1/B2/Stage C remain unapproved; test 163 stays sealed, P1 unused, and T5Gemma2 closed under D-108 STOP.**
